{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg \"next user|implicit|user_prompt\" packages/pi-lhc/test/capture docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core -n'","aggregated_output":"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:69:      \"user_prompt\",\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:106:      \"user_prompt\",\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:171:    const result = await capture([validEvent(\"user_prompt\")], deadInstance);\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:20:- An **intake event** is the unit of capture. New traffic enters as ordered intake events; LHC records them durably. The seven event kinds are `user_prompt`, `assistant_text`, `assistant_thinking`, `tool_call`, `tool_result`, `runtime_note`, and `turn_end`.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:155:  E->>L: user_prompt event (opens LHC turn)\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:167:**AC-2.2:** LHC turn boundaries are derived from PI traffic, not from PI's per-agent-step `turn_end`. One LHC turn spans a user prompt and all subsequent agent activity until the next user prompt or the end of the agent run. The converter emits exactly one LHC `turn_end` event per LHC turn, at the agent run's completion — never one per PI `turn_end`, and never keyed off PI's per-agent-run `turnIndex` as a session counter.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:264:| `user_prompt` | `{ text }` |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:276:| user `[text]` | one `user_prompt` |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:294:- An LHC turn **opens** on a `user_prompt` event.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:296:- It **closes** with one LHC `turn_end` event when the agent run completes (no further tool calls; PI's `agent_end`), or implicitly when the next `user_prompt` arrives.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:315:user_prompt, assistant_thinking, tool_call, tool_call, tool_result, tool_result,\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/support.ts:39: *  deterministic provider, so a captured user_prompt's queued derivation has a\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:99:    expect(kindsOf(events)).toEqual([\"user_prompt\", \"tool_call\", \"tool_result\", \"assistant_text\", \"turn_end\"]);\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts:67:      \"user_prompt\",\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts:104:      \"user_prompt\",\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts:107:      \"user_prompt\",\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts:126:    acc.onMessage([validEvent(\"user_prompt\")]);\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts:142:    acc.onMessage([validEvent(\"user_prompt\")]);\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts:144:    acc.onMessage([validEvent(\"user_prompt\")]);\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts:166:    expect(kindsOf(events)).toEqual([\"user_prompt\"]);\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation.md:41:**AC-2.2:** LHC turn boundaries are derived from PI traffic, not from PI's per-agent-step `turn_end`. One LHC turn spans a user prompt and all subsequent agent activity until the next user prompt or the end of the agent run. The converter emits exactly one LHC `turn_end` event per LHC turn, at the agent run's completion — never one per PI `turn_end`, and never keyed off PI's per-agent-run `turnIndex` as a session counter.\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts:57:    const a = eventKey({ piSessionId: \"s\", blockIndex: 0, kind: \"user_prompt\", role: \"user\", content: \"hello\" });\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts:58:    const aAgain = eventKey({ piSessionId: \"s\", blockIndex: 0, kind: \"user_prompt\", role: \"user\", content: \"hello\" });\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts:59:    const b = eventKey({ piSessionId: \"s\", blockIndex: 0, kind: \"user_prompt\", role: \"user\", content: \"world\" });\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/abort.test.ts:48:      \"user_prompt\",\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts:40:  return events.filter((event) => event.eventKind === \"user_prompt\").map(textOf);\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts:106:      \"user_prompt\",\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts:109:      \"user_prompt\",\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:276:The converter is three pieces. `map-message.ts` is pure: it takes one `AgentMessage` and returns the ordered events for it — a user message becomes one `user_prompt`; an assistant message fans out to `assistant_thinking` (if present), then `assistant_text` (if present), then one `tool_call` per call, in that order; a tool result becomes one `tool_result` correlated to its call by `toolCallId`, carrying `isError` when the tool failed. `turn-accumulator.ts` holds the open-turn state and decides when to emit the single `turn_end`. `converter.ts` orchestrates, batches the events, and flushes them through `intakeStream.messageEvents`, isolating failures so writable-thread failures become recorded gaps and store-unavailable failures become extension diagnostics rather than thrown exceptions.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:282:  turn_start(0)                          user_prompt\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:305:  CV->>IS: [user_prompt]\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/004-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"dcbc4543-77eb-48ca-ae16-47342b85f1a1\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec517-957e-7520-99ad-8c58c7c12cc1\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec517-957e-7520-99ad-8c58c7c12cc1\",\"storyId\":\"02-event-