n./packages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:2:// plus lazy-init and read-path-equivalence supplementals). TC-1.4 is owned by\\n./packages/lhc/test/threads.test.ts:196:  it(\\\"lazy-init supplemental: resolve against an absent registry returns thread_not_found and creates nothing\\\", async () => {\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/coverage.md:49:37/37 ACs owned · 33/33 TCs owned · 0 unassigned. Story 0 owns no epic ACs; its acceptance is FC-0.1 through FC-0.7 (foundation criteria, numbered in its file).\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/coverage.md:108:- **Story 0 owns no behavior** and proves the gates themselves (FC-numbered). Its fixture builders are golden-shaped until Story 2's schemas exist, then validated against them — recorded in both stories.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/test-plan.md:18:Fixture: Epic 03's tool-heavy fixture reused; extended in place (Story 2) with a mutation-in-flight variant — one edit applied, drain *not* settled, so cleared-pending states are real production states, not hand-written rows (FC-fidelity rule carried from Epic 03 Story 0: states reached through intake → mutate → partial drain, never direct `derived_form` writes).\\n./packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/validate.ts:4:// property of the definitions, not a remembered rule. Validation never touches\\n./packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/cascade.ts:256:// The message-delete validation refuses turn-initiating prompts, so the turn\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/epic.md:63:- Epic 03's Story 0 fixture (deterministic provider, ~12 turns, 4 chunks, tool-heavy middle, manufactured failure states) is reusable here and extends with mutation-in-flight states; no new fixture family.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/epic.md:196:No Story 0, decided not defaulted: Story-0s exist to land shared substrate that multiple stories would otherwise each half-build — migrations, new tables, config plumbing,