y: `pi-lhc-fixture-${keyCounter}`,\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:16:| `message_end` | finalized `user` / `assistant` / `toolResult` message | Map → intake event batch → `sdk.intakeStream.messageEvents` |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:36:- `message_end` handlers may replace the message; other extensions' mutations are visible — extension ordering matters if anything else mutates context.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:37:- Parallel tool mode: `tool_execution_*` events interleave, but final `toolResult` `message_end` events still arrive in assistant source order — intake ordering is safe if we drive everything off `message_end`.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:41:The POC (`pi-extension.ts`, ~2,900 lines) wires: `session_start` (snapshot ctx, reconcile rollout, hydrate truncation state), `message_end` (capture → side-channel tool-result restore → schedule smoothing → buffer truncation observation), `tool_result` (stash original content before PI/extension truncation), `turn_end` (finalize turn, parallel intake, observe/refresh projection, schedule background maintenance), `agent_end` (refresh projection), `context` (apply prompt-visible truncation), plus ~12 `lh-*` commands.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:44:- The event-to-record mapper (`pi-message-mapper.ts`) is a complete worked example of PI message → canonical mapping: role→kind mapping, content-part fan-out (text/thinking/toolCall/image/fileRef/unknown), idempotency key construction (`pi:<session>:entry:<entryId>`, responseId/toolCallId fallbacks, content fingerprint last resort), token telemetry extraction from assistant `usage`. The new converter reimplements this against `MessageEventInput` (which is far simpler — 7 event kinds, text-only payloads).\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:47:- Side-channel capture of original tool results before truncation (`tool_result` event fires before `message_end`).\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:64:message_end ────────────────────► map message → event batch ────► intakeStream.messageEvents(ref, events)\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:79:**Event mapping (the converter contract):** PI `message_end` fans out to `MessageEventInput`s:\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:84:- idempotency keys from session entry id (the POC's `targetEventKey` scheme, simplified)\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:116:     → message_start/message_end (user [text])\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:117:     → message_start/message_end (assistant [thinking?, text?, toolCall×N])\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:119:     → message_start/message_end (toolResult [text]) ×N\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:127:- **Parallel tool calls.** All N calls arrive in *one* assistant `message_end` (content = `[toolCall, toolCall, toolCall]`), each `{type,id,name,arguments}`. `tool_execution_start` events interleave and `tool_result`s complete out of order, but each `toolResult` `message_end` carries its `toolCallId`, so ordering is recoverable by ID, not arrival. Fan-out to LHC `tool_call` events is per-content-part, exactly as the mapper assumed.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:129:- **toolCallId shape.** Composite: `call_<providerId>|fc_<internalId>`. Stable across `tool_execution_start` → `tool_result` → the `toolResult` message. Usable as the correlation key and as part of the idempotency key.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:130:- **Resume/dedup — the big one.** Reopening an existing session (`--session-id` of a prior session) does **NOT** re-fire historical `message_end` events. Only the new turn's events fire (verified: 4 message events, not 10). PI loads prior history internally and exposes it through the **`context` hook** (first context on resume already held all 7 prior messages). **Consequence: LHC intake never sees duplicate historical events on resume — the dedup concern is far smaller than feared.** Idempotency keys still matter for `/reload` and crash-replay, but normal resume is clean by construction.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:136:**Hard-kill abort, captured solo:** `kill -9` mid-stream left the log at `session_start → before_agent_start → agent_start → turn_start → message_end(user)` — **no assistant `message_end`, no `turn_end`, no `agent_end`, no `session_shutdown`.** The incomplete-turn shape: user prompt captured, no agent response, turn never closed. LHC reattach after a crash finds an open turn with a trailing user prompt; intake must tolerate it. This is the crash-safety shape AC-1.4 needs.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:149:- **Graceful interrupt (Esc):** the partial assistant message gets a normal `message_end` with content preserved (`[thinking, text]`, ~120 lines kept) and **`stopReason: \"aborted\"`**; `turn_end` fires, also `stopReason: \"aborted\"`; `agent_end` fires. A graceful abort is a *complete, well-formed turn marked aborted* — partial content is real and worth keeping. The session continues normally on the next prompt (verified: follow-up ran `stopReason: \"stop\"`, no recovery path).\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:150:- **Hard-kill (`kill -9`, §5a):** nothing closes — user `message_end` only, no assistant close, no `turn_end`. Dangling open turn.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:163:- **Resume re-fires zero `message_end` events** (confirmed interactively, matching §5a) — history served via `context` only. Dedup is needed for `/reload` + crash-replay, not normal resume.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/notes/pi-ext-integration-research.md:191:**Epic A — Connector core (intake + lifecycle + inference host):** ~5–6 stories. SDK construction/teardown on session lifecycle, thread mapping + resume/reload/fork handling, message/turn event mapper (converter productionized), `ModelCall` + assignments config + startup validation, ordering/idempotency proof against recorded corpora.\npackages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.test.ts:44:  it(\"build correctly-typed LHC intake events with unique idempotency keys\", () => {\npackages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.test.ts:47:    const keys = batch.map((e) => e.idempotencyKey);\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-tech-arch.md:80:| Event Capture | PI message/turn events → LHC intake batches (the converter, productionized); ordering, idempotency, dedup | PI `message_end`/`turn_end`, LHC intakeStream | Epic 1. The one mapper. No other surface writes intake events. |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-tech-arch.md:184:- **Transport:** PI `message_end` and `turn_end` events → Event Capture maps each to one or more LHC `MessageEventInput`s → `intakeStream.messageEvents(ref, batch)`.\npackages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:19:  | \"message_end\"\npackages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:60:  entryId: string;\npackages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:78:  message_end: MessageEndEvent;\npackages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:177:  /** Composite, stable across tool_execution_start → tool_result → message_end\npackages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:194:    if (typeof ev.idempotencyKey !== \"string\" || ev.idempotencyKey === \"\") problems.push(`${at}: empty idempotencyKey`);\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md:8:- Last Completed Checkpoint: Story 1 committed (6a7d95b). Story 2: implement 003 (40m, OK) wrote full converter+turn-derivation+idempotency+runtime-changes+index wiring + test/capture (on disk). Verify 004 = revise, ONE critical finding SV-001 (\"existing-thread resume/reload can silently skip new finalized events\"). Continue 005 (fixing SV-001, ~1MB output) FAILED at finalize = PROVIDER_OUTPUT_INVALID (recurring claude-code large-continue/session-resume parse flaki