ers/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/package.json\",\"manual node reproduction: resume/reload idempotency collision using built packages/pi-lhc/dist/index.js\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Initial verification covered Story 2 AC/TC requirements, Flow 2 tech design, capture/runtime production paths, Story 2 tests, configured gates, and manual existing-thread reattach scenarios.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"Existing-thread resume/reload can silently skip new finalized events\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.1 requires every finalized PI message to be recorded exactly once, and AC-2.6/TC-2.7 require duplicate safety without normal-resume historical replay. On every session_start, createConnector resets captureSession.sourceSeq to 0 in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:310-318; nextEntryId then returns s0, s1, ... in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:352-357; message/runtime hooks use that generated entryId in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:362-384. eventKey gives entryId first precedence in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:35-40, so a fresh connector attached to an existing thread reuses prior keys. Manual reproduction against the built production connector: after recording user_prompt 'first', starting a fresh connector with --session for the same thread and recording user_prompt 'second after resume', intakeStream.listEvents returned only the first event with key pi:th_947f6dd71f50d513:entry:s0:0:user_prompt and connector diag was null. The same reload shape returned only the first event with key pi:th_d1fc3d71df1144d3:entry:s0:0:user_prompt. Existing TC-2.7 coverage in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:108-153 only proves identical batch re-delivery skips; it does not prove normal resume/reload continues recording new events.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/p