roduction connector: after recording user_prompt 'first', starting a fresh connector with --session for the same thread and recording user_prompt 'second after resume', intakeStream.listEvents returned only the first event with key pi:th_947f6dd71f50d513:entry:s0:0:user_prompt and connector diag was null. The same reload shape returned only the first event with key pi:th_d1fc3d71df1144d3:entry:s0:0:user_prompt. Existing TC-2.7 coverage in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:108-153 only proves identical batch re-delivery skips; it does not prove normal resume/reload continues recording new events.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:496:          - \"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:498:          - \"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:535:        command: \"manual node --input-type=module existing-thread resume/reload idempotency reproduction\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:538:      - \"Production capture path uses real LHC intakeStream.messageEvents, but reattach state is not durable: sourceSeq and turn_end closedCount reset for every fresh connector, making new events on existing threads collide with prior idempotency keys.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:585:    planSummary: \"Implemented Story 2 (Event Capture and Turn Derivation) — Chunk 2 — TDD Red→Green. Red: wrote 5 capture test files driving the production hook→converter→real-LHC-intake path plus direct unit calls, confirmed all 21 fail for the right reason against the fail-closed skeletons (never asserting on NotImplementedError), and froze them in red-manifest.json. Green: implemented idempotency.eventKey (precedence entryId→toolCallId→responseId→content-fingerprint), the pure map-message (assistant fan-out thinking→text→tool_call, tool_result correlation by toolCallId with error flag, unsupported parts and empty messages degrade to runtime_note, graceful-interrupt disposition carried on a trailing runtime_note), the TurnAccumulator (open-turn tracking; exactly one turn_end at agent_end; replay-stable turn keys; hard-kill leaves the turn open), runtime-changes (model_select/thinking_level_select → ordered runtime_notes carrying new+previous), and converter.capture (failure isolation: invalid_event on a writable thread records a durable gap runtime_note; store-unavailable surfaces as a structured error, never a throw). Wired index.ts message_end/model_select/thinking_level_select/agent_end to the converter with per-session capture state (open-turn accumulator + monotonic source-event index) and mapped failures into SessionState.health; PI per-step turn_end stays a no-op (ignored as an LHC boundary).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:588:        path: \"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:604:        reason: \"Wired the capture hook rail (message_end/model_select/thinking_level_select/agent_end) through map→accumulate→converter into real LHC intake; added per-session capture state (accumulator + source-event index) in the closure; mapped capture failures into SessionState.health (recordedGap true on invalid_event, false on store-unavailable); turn_end remains a no-op.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:618:        path: \"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:619:        reason: \"NEW — deterministic eventKey precedence goldens + the idempotency architecture-risk corpus double-replay (no duplicate events; re-delivered keys skipped).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:635:        - \"test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:660:        - \"Confirmed PI per-step turn_end and agent_end carry content redundant with message_end, so the converter maps only message_end content and treats turn_end/agent_end as signals — avoiding double-capture.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:666:      - \"When PI's real entry id / provider response id are exposed on the message_end hook, they should replace the converter's synthesized source-event index in the idempotency key (they slot into the existing higher-precedence tiers). Until then the synthesized index is the entry id.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:673:      - \"(5) the converter synthesizes a per-session entry index as the idempotency entry id because PI's real entry id is not in the declared hook slice yet.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:744:Latest note highlight: Next planner turn should evaluate the implementor artifact against TC-2.1 through TC-2.9 plus idempotency and atomicity risk tests before choosing review or verify.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:747:- sequence=4; actionSequence=3; createdAt=2026-06-14T07:04:54.795Z; note=\"Next planner turn should evaluate the implementor artifact against TC-2.1 through TC-2.9 plus idempotency and atomicity risk tests before choosing review or verify.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:782:    selfNote: \"Next planner turn should evaluate the implementor artifact against TC-2.1 through TC-2.9 plus idempotency and atomicity risk tests before choosing review or verify.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:790:    note: \"Next planner turn should evaluate the implementor artifact against TC-2.1 through TC-2.9 plus idempotency and atomicity risk tests before choosing review or verify.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:38:- Productionized converter from PI `message_end` and runtime-selection hooks to LHC `MessageEventInput` events.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:58:**AC-2.1:** Every PI message finalized through `message_end` — user, assistant, tool result — is mapped to LHC intake events and recorded in source order. An assistant message fans out to per-content-part events in thinking → text → tool-call order: `assistant_thinking`, `assistant_text`, and one `tool_call` per call.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:80:**AC-2.6:** Capture is duplicate-safe. Re-delivered events (reload, crash-replay) are recognized by idempotency key and skipped rather than recorded twice. On normal resume PI re-delivers no historical events, so duplication only arises on the reload and replay paths.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:82:**TC-2.7** — A re-delivered event (reload/replay) is skipped by idempotency key; a normal resume re-delivers no historical events.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:99:The source of order is the converter's source-event order. This story also owns runtime-change capture, idempotency keys, and capture failure isolation.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:121:| Idempotency | `packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts` |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:124:| Tests | `packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts`, `packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts`, `packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts`, `packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/abort.test.ts`, `packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts` |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:147:| TC-2.7 | `test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts` | Re-delivered event is skipped by idempotency key; normal resume does not replay historical messages. |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:155:| Idempotency / Retry | `test/capture/idempotency.test.ts` | Replaying the same corpus twice produces no duplicate events; re-delivered keys return `skipped`. | Single-event dedup does not prove reload/replay safety across a corpus. |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-captu