parts and empty messages degrade to runtime_note, graceful-interrupt disposition carried on a trailing runtime_note), the TurnAccumulator (open-turn tracking; exactly one turn_end at agent_end; replay-stable turn keys; hard-kill leaves the turn open), runtime-changes (model_select/thinking_level_select → ordered runtime_notes carrying new+previous), and converter.capture (failure isolation: invalid_event on a writable thread records a durable gap runtime_note; store-unavailable surfaces as a structured error, never a throw). Wired index.ts message_end/model_select/thinking_level_select/agent_end to the converter with per-session capture state (open-turn accumulator + monotonic source-event index) and mapped failures into SessionState.health; PI per-step turn_end stays a no-op (ignored as an LHC boundary).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:465:        reason: \"Wired the capture hook rail (message_end/model_select/thinking_level_select/agent_end) through map→accumulate→converter into real LHC intake; added per-session capture state (accumulator + source-event index) in the closure; mapped capture failures into SessionState.health (recordedGap true on invalid_event, false on store-unavailable); turn_end remains a no-op.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:521:        - \"Confirmed PI per-step turn_end and agent_end carry content redundant with message_end, so the converter maps only message_end content and treats turn_end/agent_end as signals — avoiding double-capture.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:527:      - \"When PI's real entry id / provider response id are exposed on the message_end hook, they should replace the converter's synthesized source-event index in the idempotency key (they slot into the existing higher-precedence tiers). Until then the synthesized index is the entry id.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:38:- Productionized converter from PI `message_end` and runtime-selection hooks to LHC `MessageEventInput` events.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:58:**AC-2.1:** Every PI message finalized through `message_end` — user, assistant, tool result — is mapped to LHC intake events and recorded in source order. An assistant message fans out to per-content-part events in thinking → text → tool-call order: `assistant_thinking`, `assistant_text`, and one `tool_call` per call.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:173:- Entrypoint: PI `message_end`, `turn_end`, `agent_end`, `model_select`, and `thinking_level_select` hooks routed through `index.ts`.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:475:        evidence: \"AC-2.1 requires every finalized PI message to be recorded exactly once, and AC-2.6/TC-2.7 require duplicate safety without normal-resume historical replay. On every session_start, createConnector resets captureSession.sourceSeq to 0 in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:310-318; nextEntryId then returns s0, s1, ... in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:352-357; message/runtime hooks use that generated entryId in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:362-384. eventKey gives entryId first precedence in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:35-40, so a fresh connector attached to an existing thread reuses prior keys. Manual reproduction against the built production connector: after recording user_prompt 'first', starting a fresh connector with --session for the same thread and recording user_prompt 'second after resume', intakeStream.listEvents returned only the first event with key pi:th_947f6dd71f50d513:entry:s0:0:user_prompt and connector diag was null. The same reload shape returned only the first event with key pi:th_d1fc3d71df1144d3:entry:s0:0:user_prompt. Existing TC-2.7 coverage in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:108-153 only proves identical batch re-delivery skips; it does not prove normal resume/reload continues recording new events.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:493:        evidence: \"AC-2.1 requires every finalized PI message to be recorded exactly once, and AC-2.6/TC-2.7 require duplicate safety without normal-resume historical replay. On every session_start, createConnector resets captureSession.sourceSeq to 0 in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:310-318; nextEntryId then returns s0, s1, ... in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:352-357; message/runtime hooks use that generated entryId in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:362-384. eventKey gives entryId first precedence in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:35-40, so a fresh connector attached to an existing thread reuses prior keys. Manual reproduction against the built production connector: after recording user_prompt 'first', starting a fresh connector with --session for the same thread and recording user_prompt 'second after resume', intakeStream.listEvents returned only the first event with key pi:th_947f6dd71f50d513:entry:s0:0:user_prompt and connector diag was null. The same reload shape returned only the first event with key pi:th_d1fc3d71df1144d3:entry:s0:0:user_prompt. Existing TC-2.7 coverage in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:108-153 only proves identical batch re-delivery skips; it does not prove normal resume/reload continues recording new events.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:585:    planSummary: \"Implemented Story 2 (Event Capture and Turn Derivation) — Chunk 2 — TDD Red→Green. Red: wrote 5 capture test files driving the production hook→converter→real-LHC-intake path plus direct unit calls, confirmed all 21 fail for the right reason against the fail-closed skeletons (never asserting on NotImplementedError), and froze them in red-manifest.json. Green: implemented idempotency.eventKey (precedence entryId→toolCallId→responseId→content-fingerprint), the pure map-message (assistant fan-out thinking→text→tool_call, tool_result correlation by toolCallId with error flag, unsupported parts and empty messages degrade to runtime_note, graceful-interrupt disposition carried on a trailing runtime_note), the TurnAccumulator (open-turn tracking; exactly one turn_end at agent_end; replay-stable turn keys; hard-kill leaves the turn open), runtime-changes (model_select/thinking_level_select → ordered runtime_notes carrying new+previous), and converter.capture (failure isolation: invalid_event on a writable thread records a durable gap runtime_note; store-unavailable surfaces as a structured error, never a throw). Wired index.ts message_end/model_select/thinking_level_select/agent_end to the converter with per-session capture state (open-turn accumulator + monotonic source-event index) and mapped failures into SessionState.health; PI per-step turn_end stays a no-op (ignored as an LHC boundary).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:604:        reason: \"Wired the capture hook rail (message_end/model_select/thinking_level_select/agent_end) through map→accumulate→converter into real LHC intake; added per-session capture state (accumulator + source-event index) in the closure; mapped capture failures into SessionState.health (recordedGap true on invalid_event, false on store-unavailable); turn_end remains a no-op.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:660:        - \"Confirmed PI per-step turn_end and agent_end carry content redundant with message_end, so the converter maps only message_end content and treats turn_end/agent_end as signals — avoiding double-capture.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:666:      - \"When PI's real entry id / provider response id are exposed on the message_end hook, they should replace the converter's synthesized source-event index in the idempotency key (they slot into the existing higher-precedence tiers). Until then the synthesized index is the entry id.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:38:- Productionized converter from PI `message_end` and runtime-selection hooks to LHC `MessageEventInput` events.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:58:**AC-2.1:** Every PI message finalized through `message_end` — user, assistant, tool result — is mapped to LHC intake events and recorded in source order. An assistant message fans out to per-content-part events in thinking → text → tool-call order: `assistant_thinking`, `assistant_text`, and one `tool_call` per call.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:173:- Entrypoint: PI `message_end`, `turn_end`, `agent_end`, `model_select`, and `thinking_level_select` hooks routed through `index.ts`.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:475:        evidence: \"AC-2.1 requires every finalized PI message to be recorded exactly once, and AC-2.6/TC-2.7 r