m as an ordered time series and make boundary decisions from position in that stream.\\\\n./docs/onboard/02-domain-design.md:239:Delete is a projection-level operation. The message drops from reads and from its turn's membership, but the source events it was created from stay in the event log; the record underneath is never destroyed. Deleting a message that initiates a turn is refused — a turn is a prompt and what came back for it, so removing the prompt means removing the turn, and that goes through the `turns` surface as an explicit turn delete instead of hiding behind a one-message operation.\\\\n./packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:132:// from Story 0; the operation shapes land with Stories 1–5.\\\\n./packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:244:// §Interface Definitions): the operations only — the Story 0 config\\\\n./packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:285:  if (!Number.isFinite(value) || value <= 0) {\\\\n./packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:291:  if (!Number.isFinite(value) || value < 0) {\\\\n./packages/pi-lhc/test/smoke/extension-load.test.ts:4:import { initInstance } from \\\\\\\"../../src/lifecycle/instance.js\\\\\\\";\\\\n./packages/pi-lhc/test/smoke/extension-load.test.ts:86:  it(\\\\\\\"exposes a stubbed init/dispose seam that returns a typed fail-closed result\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n./packages/pi-lhc/test/smoke/extension-load.test.ts:87:    const result = await initInstance({ filePath: \\\\\\\"/tmp/thread.sqlite\\\\\\\" }, { mode: \\\\\\\"background\\\\\\\" });\\\\n./packages/pi-lhc/test/smoke/extension-load.test.ts:90:      expect(result.error.code).toBe(\\\\\\\"not_implemented\\\\\\\");\\\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/team-impl-log.md:9:- Story 0 accepted and committed: f89f794 (manual impl-lead acceptance; story-run record stuck needs-ruling due to CLI ruling-application bug — see Open Risks)\\\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/team-impl-log.md:28:- Gate Discovery Rationale: Gates taken verbatim from the spec pack's per-story Verification sections (