es/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/state.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/validate.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/abort.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/support.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts\",\"manual node --input-type=module reload redelivery reproduction against packages/pi-lhc/dist/index.js\",\"manual node --input-type=module malformed-gap inspect.health reproduction against packages/pi-lhc/dist and packages/lhc/dist\",\"manual node --input-type=module unsupported toolResult fileRef mapping check\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Initial verification covered Story 2 AC/TC requirements, Flow 2 tech design, production capture/idempotency/failure paths, Story 2 tests, configured gates, and targeted manual reproductions for reload redelivery, health surfacing, and unsupported content handling.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"Reload/crash-replay redelivery records duplicates instead of skipping them\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.6 and TC-2.7 require redelivered reload/replay events to be skipped by the same idempotency key. The production connector seeds captureSession.sourceSeq from inspect.overview event count on session_start (packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:312-326), then generates new entry ids from that counter for message/runtime hooks (packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:364-378). TurnAccumulator likewise seeds turn_end keys from closed turn count (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts:35-62). Because eventKey gives entryId first precedence (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:38-44), a redelivered historical message after reload gets a new key instead of the original key. Manual reproduction against built production code: after recording user_prompt 'first' and turn_end, a reload redelivering the same user message produced four stored events [user_prompt, turn_end, user_prompt, turn_end] with keys s0/turn:0 and s2/turn:1; connector diagnostic was null. Existing reattach tests prove new post-resume messages record, but do not prove reload/crash-replay historical redelivery skips.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"AC-2.6\",\"TC-2.7\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Writable capture gaps are not surfaced in thread health\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.7 and TC-2.8 require a malformed/unmappable event on a writable thread to record a durable, queryable gap that surfaces in thread health. capture() records the gap as a runtime_note (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts:48-56) and connector state records lastCaptureFailure (packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:344-358), but inspect health is composed only from message/turn form reports (packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts:40-108). The current test asserts only listEvents contains a runtime_note (packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:149-158), not inspect.health. Manual reproduction after capture([malformed turn_end]) showed the runtime_note gap in listEvents, while inspect.health returned owners=[], failures=[], repairPreview=[], queue={queued:0,claimed:0}.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.7\",\"TC-2.8\",\"Atomicity / Isolation\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-003\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Unsupported tool-result content parts are silently omitted\",\"evidence\":\"The story risk reminders and tech design require unsupported image/file-reference parts to record an omission rather than vanish silently. map-message.ts defines unsupportedOf/omissionText and uses them for user and assistant messages (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts:52-61, 131-168), but mapToolResult only joins text parts and emits one tool_result (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts:185-197). Manual mapMessage({role:'toolResult', toolCallId:'call_file', content:[{type:'fileRef', path:'/tmp/out.png'}]}) returned only tool_result with content:'' and no runtime_note omission.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"TechDesign-I-6\",\"Production Path Audit\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"title\":\"Reload/crash-replay redelivery records duplicates instead of skipping them\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.6 and TC-2.7 require redelivered reload/replay events to be skipped by the same idempotency key. The production connector seeds captureSession.sourceSeq from inspect.overview event count on session_start (packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:312-326), then generates new entry ids from that counter for message/runtime hooks (packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:364-378). TurnAccumulator likewise seeds turn_end keys from closed turn count (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts:35-62). Because eventKey gives entryId first precedence (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:38-44), a redelivered historical message after reload gets a new key instead of the original key. Manual reproduction against built production code: after recording user_prompt 'first' and turn_end, a reload redelivering the same user message produced four stored events [user_prompt, turn_end, user_prompt, turn_end] with keys s0/turn:0 and s2/turn:1; connector diagnostic was null. Existing reattach tests prove new post-resume messages record, but do not prove reload/crash-replay historical redelivery skips.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"AC-2.6\",\"TC-2.7\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Writable capture gaps are not surfaced in thread health\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.7 and TC-2.8 require a malformed/unmappable event on a writable thread to record a durable, queryable gap that surfaces in thread health. capture() records the gap as a runtime_note (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts:48-56) and connector state records lastCaptureFailure (packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:344-358), but inspect health is composed only from message/turn form reports (packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts:40-108). The current test asserts only listEvents contains a runtime_note (packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:149-158), not inspect.health. Manual reproduction after capture([malformed turn_end]) showed the runtime_note gap in listEvents, while inspect.health returned owners=[], failures=[], repairPreview=[], queue={queued:0,claimed:0}.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.7\",\"TC-2.8\",\"Atomicity / Isolation\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-003\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Unsupported tool-result content parts are silently omitted\",\"evidence\":\"The story risk reminders and tech design require unsupported image/file-reference parts to record an omission rather than vanish silently. map-message.ts defines unsupportedOf/omissionText and uses them for user and assistant messages (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts:52-61, 131-168), but mapToolResult only joins text parts and emits one tool_result (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts:185-197). Manual mapMessage({role:'toolResult', toolCallId:'call_file', content:[{type:'fileRef', path:'/tmp/out.png'}]}) returned only tool_result with content:'' and no runtime_note omission.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"TechDesign-I-6\",\"Production Path Audit\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-2.1 / TC-2.1 happy-path user, assistant, and toolResult capture in source order with assistant thinking -> text -> tool_call fan-out.\",\"AC-2.2 / TC-2.2 / TC-2.3 PI per-step turn_end is ignored, LHC turn_end is emitted at agent_end, and repeated turnIndex values do not drive ordering.\",\"AC-2.3 / TC-2.4 parallel tool results carry toolCallId and preserve out-of-order arrival without arrival-order correlation.\",\"AC-2.4 / TC-2.5 error tool result captures content with isError true.\",\"AC-2.5 / TC-2.6 graceful interrupt captures partial assistant content, carries aborted disposition, and closes the turn at agent_end.\",\"AC-2.8 / TC-2.9 model_select and thinking_level_select are captured as ordered runtime_note events with previous and new values.\",\"Direct same-key capture() batch reflush dedups through LHC intakeStream and returns skipped duplicate_idempotency_key outcomes.\",\"Story gate pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify passed.\",\"Epic gate pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all passed.\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-2.6 / TC-2.7 production hook-level reload and crash-replay redelivery: manual reproduction shows duplicates, not skips.\",\"AC-2.7 / TC-2.8 thread-health surfacing for durable writable capture gaps: manual reproduction shows inspect.health does not report the gap.\",\"TechDesign-I-6 unsupported image/file-reference omission coverage for toolResult messages: code audit and manual mapper call show omission is not recorded.\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"manual node --input-type=module reload redelivery reproduction against packages/pi-lhc/dist/index.js\",\"result\":\"fail\"},{\"command\":\"manual node --input-type=module malformed-gap inspect.health reproduction against packages/pi-lhc/dist and packages/lhc/dist\",\"result\":\"fail\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"Production connector idempotency currently uses attach-time event/turn counts as the generated entry-id seed; that fixes normal resume append collisions but breaks reload/crash-replay redelivery dedup by assigning historical events new keys.\",\"Writable-thread capture failure is persisted as a runtime_note but is not represented in LHC inspect.health, so the durable gap is queryable only as a generic event log entry, not as thread health.\",\"mapToolResult silently drops non-text fileRef/image parts because unsupported-part omission handling is only implemented for user and assistant messages.\",\"No material fake/mock intake path was found in Story 2 capture execution; production capture writes through real LHC intakeStream.messageEvents. Test fakes are confined to fixtures/config.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"Configured gates pass with 58 tests, but the required reload/crash-replay and health-surfacing scenarios are not covered by those tests.\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/008-verify.json exists but is zero bytes; this verification did not rely on it.\"]}"}}
